<%#
  Shown when a submitted scorecard can't be matched to an open fixture.

  Every one of these cases used to be a thrown Error landing on the 500 page, which
  prints the error's own text — so a captain resubmitting a result that had saved
  perfectly well read "no matching fixtures" and concluded it hadn't. The captain whose
  submission genuinely failed and the captain whose submission was fine saw identical,
  meaningless screens.

  Locals: conflict { reason, fixture?, candidates? }, data (the submitted body).
%>
<%- include('header.ejs') %>
<%- include('nav.ejs') %>

<div class="container" style="max-width:720px;text-align:left;margin:0 auto 48px">

<% if (conflict.reason === 'already-recorded') { %>
  <h1>This match is already recorded</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    We have it as
    <strong><%= conflict.fixture.homeScore %>&ndash;<%= conflict.fixture.awayScore %></strong><% if (conflict.fixture.date) { %>,
    played on <%= new Date(conflict.fixture.date).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' }) %><% } %>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing has been lost and you don't need to send it again. If that score is wrong,
    or you think you're looking at the wrong match, email the results secretary at
    <a href="mailto:stockport.badders.results@gmail.com">stockport.badders.results@gmail.com</a>
    and say which fixture you mean.
  </p>
  <p><a class="btn btn-success" href="/event/<%= conflict.fixture.id %>">See the recorded result</a></p>

<% } else if (conflict.reason === 'rearranged') { %>
  <h1>That fixture has been rearranged</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The match you've entered was marked as rearranged, so there's no open fixture for it
    on that date.
  </p>
  <p>
    If it has now been played, the new date needs to be in the system before the result
    can go in. Email
    <a href="mailto:stockport.badders.results@gmail.com">stockport.badders.results@gmail.com</a>
    with the date it was played and your scorecard, and it'll be sorted out. Keep this
    page or a photo of the card in the meantime.
  </p>

<% } else if (conflict.reason === 'conceded') { %>
  <h1>That fixture is recorded as conceded</h1>
  <p class="lead">There's no open fixture to attach a score to.</p>
  <p>
    If the match was actually played, email
    <a href="mailto:stockport.badders.results@gmail.com">stockport.badders.results@gmail.com</a>
    with the details and it can be reopened.
  </p>

<% } else if (conflict.reason === 'ambiguous') { %>
  <h1>We can't tell which match this is</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    There's more than one open fixture between these two teams, and the date you entered
    doesn't single one out:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <% conflict.candidates.forEach(function(c) { %>
      <li><%= new Date(c.date).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { weekday: 'long', day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' }) %></li>
    <% }) %>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Rather than guess and put your result against the wrong night, we've stopped. Go back
    and set the match date to the one you played, and submit again.
  </p>
  <p><a class="btn btn-success" href="/scorecard-beta">Back to the scorecard</a></p>

<% } else if (conflict.reason === 'bad-total') { %>
  <h1>Those scores don't add up to a match</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A league fixture is 18 games, so the two totals should come to 18. You've entered
    <strong><%= conflict.homeScore %></strong> and <strong><%= conflict.awayScore %></strong><% if (conflict.total !== null) { %>,
    which is <strong><%= conflict.total %></strong><% } %>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing has been saved. Go back, check the game-by-game scores against the card, and
    submit again. If the match genuinely wasn't 18 games &mdash; a concession, say &mdash;
    email
    <a href="mailto:stockport.badders.results@gmail.com">stockport.badders.results@gmail.com</a>
    rather than forcing it through here.
  </p>
  <p><a class="btn btn-success" href="/scorecard-beta">Back to the scorecard</a></p>

<% } else { %>
  <h1>We can't find that fixture</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    There's no fixture in this season between those two teams, so there's nothing to
    record the result against.
  </p>
  <p>
    Check the two teams are the right way round &mdash; home team first &mdash; and that
    you've picked the right sides. If they look right, email
    <a href="mailto:stockport.badders.results@gmail.com">stockport.badders.results@gmail.com</a>
    and include the date and the score.
  </p>
  <p><a class="btn btn-success" href="/scorecard-beta">Back to the scorecard</a></p>
<% } %>

</div>

<%- include('footer.ejs') %>

</body>
</html>
